<!doctype html><html lang="zh-CN"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>1390 training layout and pyramid entry</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#101a29;color:#e7edf7;font:16px/1.8 "Microsoft YaHei",sans-serif}main{max-width:1150px;margin:auto;padding:24px}a{color:#9fd5ff}nav{position:sticky;top:0;background:#172638;padding:12px;z-index:2;display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap}pre{overflow:auto;background:#09131f;padding:16px}code{font:13px/1.7 Consolas,monospace}table{border-collapse:collapse;display:block;overflow:auto}td,th{border:1px solid #45617e;padding:8px 12px}blockquote{border-left:4px solid #e7b667;margin:18px 0;padding:1px 16px;background:#203249}h1,h2,h3,h4{scroll-margin-top:85px}img{max-width:100%}.meta{font-size:12px;color:#a9bfd3;overflow-wrap:anywhere}summary{cursor:pointer}</style><nav><a href="../../../framework-architecture.html">主架构</a><a href="../../main-ui-map.html">逆向核心</a><a href="../index.html">关联文档目录</a><a data-source-download download href="../../../plugins/GRAY-MATCH-1390-TRAINING-PYRAMID-SOURCE.md">下载原始文件</a></nav><main><h1 id="1390-training-layout-and-pyramid-entry">1390 training layout and pyramid entry</h1><h2 id="production-implementation-update">Production implementation update</h2><p>Root-approved caller pyramid is now <code>src/VisionPlugins.GrayMatch/GrayMatchTrainingPyramid.cs</code>, SHA67060E52A713F331A025BBCC2879E84B81D8A0B1F2F3621BC9E1AB60DA0E83B5. <code>normalizedRequestedLevels</code> is explicitly1..8: training raw0→8 belongs to the original upstream trainer, while search has its own normalized count. API rejects raw0 and tests this precondition; it does not silently change search semantics.</p>
<p>Production ProjectReference checks passed84, including a separately approved original65x65 tight chain through33x33/17x17/9x9 for both actual image kernels and the mask kernel, with every level compared byte-for-byte. The one-layer padded fixture compares against original <strong>tight</strong> leaf bytes after caller copy. Necessary regressions Model125/Score12/Dot65/Policy13 also passed, five final builds zero warnings/errors and all runs exit0. No first-divergence tolerance adjustment. Source snapshot drift0. Manifest <code>analysis/gray-match/pyramid-managed/manifest.json</code> SHA60D645EECA9159B8F3B79D5FFE1D56B3D496B5DBD8412124FC9C15DE1F3088B2 records source/PDB/DLL/oracles/logs. Original chain manifest SHA0E73A8EB4561FD35F1412ADE92ACC86D45F822C372216E6FC461DA7E011096B7. Earlier candidate/not-run statements below are historical for this component; full training/search remain incomplete.</p>
<p>Same core SHA85D17ECC87D52E9A62D8BB86C8D5208AC999BCD31EC6D0806453F8165733F549; isolated read-only Ghidra batches <code>train-layout</code> and <code>train-pyramid</code> both exit0. Source index now41 bodies, SHA2FEDF7740911449D36C49078F20DC158807629F62C5C2F9884A4CB3C52F5127A. Raw C/asm and logs are in <code>analysis/gray-match/core-boundary</code>. No SDK initialization, device, image oracle or managed build was run.</p>
<p><code>bf38f0→befbb0→befdc0</code> is the current1390 training route. <code>befbb0</code> returns10000014 for required nulls,1000001A for nonpositive dimensions,1000001B if width exceeds either supplied stride,10000019 if requested levels&gt;8,10100001 for unsupported version. It calls <code>c97550</code>, returning10100000 when that predicate fails. The recovered predicate scans image bytes only where mask byte is nonzero; min starts INT_MAX and max INT_MIN, and it accepts signed <code>(max-min)&gt;1</code>. The all-zero mask sentinel arithmetic must retain signed modular behavior; do not replace it with a guessed variance threshold. This is a source predicate, not a claim that all low-level bad dimensions/pointers may safely execute.</p>
<p><code>befdc0</code> normalizes requested levels0 to8 (auto path), initializes model base offsets0x27700 and a second aligned pyramid block, and stores1390 at model+276b8. Each level&#39;s metadata stride is0x4ed0. It constructs angle tables with actual float addition and <code>&lt;=</code> against its computed endpoint; no integer-count replacement is established.</p>
<p><code>c96ce0</code> computes capacity with repeated <code>(dimension+1)&gt;&gt;1</code>, clamps level count by positive dimensions/products, sums each level&#39;s pixel count rounded up to128, then adds128 for version&gt;=1390. Older versions additionally allocate pointer/offset arrays; they are not the active training target. <code>c96ef0</code> computes each requested layer&#39;s ceil-half dimensions. <code>c97840</code> workspace formula is aligned128 of signed-int32 <code>((w+1)*(w+1)+(h+1)*(h+1))</code>; it is not simply image area. Overflow/safety policy must be distinct from original arithmetic.</p>
<p><code>c97090</code> has nine actual arguments: image, stride, packed dimensions, requested levels, minimum lower-layer area, version, image-versus-mask selector, output block, output pointer. Entry asm reads selector at its correct stack slot. Actual caller supplies min-area32, version1390, selector0 for image and1 for mask. It caps actual pyramid depth using that area predicate.1390 header carries count at0, dimension pairs from+0x4, offsets from+0x44 with first pixel payload+0x80. Each next layer payload is separately aligned128. Source full-resolution copy uses <code>6e7ca0</code>; output pointer aliases the supplied output block.</p>
<p>The mask path is <strong>c96f20 nearest even-coordinate decimation</strong>, not averaging: output(x,y)=input(2x,2y), output dimensions ceil-half. Image selector0 calls a distinct CPU detector <strong>62f260</strong>, then uses <code>d46a10</code> when its result&gt;=5, otherwise <code>d472b0</code>. This detector is the CPUID1 SSE feature ladder0..6, not the separate630120 class11 policy used for dot/search. Reusing that class or hardcoding11 here would misdispatch. Both image bodies are recovered; scalar C shows interior four-byte sum shifted2 and separate odd-edge two-byte shifts1, but SIMD rounding/edge assembly is not yet closed, so no backend-equivalence claim or product sampler is made.</p>
<p>Next implementation dependency is the image sampler&#39;s exact SIMD/interior/odd-edge arithmetic, followed by training angle/model-relative buffer writes and current1390 search workspace consumption. Existing41 C bodies do not mean these outputs are implemented. ModelSlots125/Score12/Dot65/Policy13 remain verified production infrastructure; full model training/search, native model file transport, runtime result publication and real plugin registration remain open.</p>
<h2 id="finite-original-leaf-confirmation-and-caller-restriction">Finite original leaf confirmation and caller restriction</h2><p>Root-approved pure leaf probe is <code>tests/GrayMatch.NativeProbe/PyramidProbe.cpp</code>: explicit five-argument ABI, same-hash DLL, enough owned input/output buffers, widths3/32/33, heights3/4, strideswidth orwidth+7.12 layouts×3 kernels produced36 outputs, native build/run0. <code>analysis/gray-match/pyramid-native/manifest.json</code> SHA856793ACE5938C7D08293FE0113E7A42473EA86C5094671FB510F295B8E3ACE8 includes raw source/asm, input bytes, output bytes, executable and replay identity. First batch-command slash invocation failure is preserved separately; final native execution completed. No initialization/device APIs were called.</p>
<p>Independent source-formula replay matches all36 outputs byte-for-byte. Image backends agree on these layouts. Interior is exact unsigned four-byte sum&gt;&gt;2; odd final row/column uses two-byte sum&gt;&gt;1; corner copies one byte. PAVGB in the older SIMD path is preceded and followed by XOR255, giving floor averaging, not its usual rounded-up result. Direct odd-column leaf behavior uses the end of <strong>stride</strong>, including padding, confirmed on four padded odd-width layouts (two bytes each differ from a conventional resize using end of width). This is entirely inside the allocated input, not an unknown heap read.</p>
<p>Crucial actual-caller restriction: c97090 copies full-resolution image into a tightly packed layer first, then passes <strong>current layer width as stride</strong> to every reduction. Thus the direct padded-leaf odd-column difference is not evidence that normal training reads source row padding. Candidate <code>analysis/gray-match/proposals/GrayMatchTrainingPyramid.cs</code> models this full caller order with immutable list transport and owned pixel arrays, source1390 relative offsets and minimum-area32 depth. It is not a vendor model serializer, does not manufacture uninitialized header bytes, and has not been compiled/run. Product source remains frozen. Next dependency is angle/model writes and search consumption; native leaf36 outputs do not close training as a whole.</p>
